extends layout
block content
  header.page-header
    h1.page-header__title About Samuel&apos;s Sermons
    hr.divider.divider--center
    p.page-header__desc Learn about Rev. Samuel Starling and the mission to preserve his spiritual legacy

  .about-intro
    img.about-intro__portrait(src='/images/samuel-starling-1.jpg' alt='Portrait of Rev. Samuel Starling' width='220')
    h2.about-intro__name Rev. Samuel Starling
    p.about-intro__role Minister &amp; Spiritual Guide

  section.about-content.section(aria-labelledby="legacy-heading")
    h2#legacy-heading.section-heading Preserving a Legacy
    p
      | This website is dedicated to the memory of my grandfather, Samuel Starling, a dedicated minister whose 
      | wisdom, kindness, and spiritual guidance touched countless lives through the Methodist church.
    p
      | When he passed away, he left behind a treasure trove of sermons—carefully crafted teachings spanning decades, 
      | with some dating back to the 1980s. These sermons are more than just words on paper; they reflect his deep desire 
      | to uplift, guide, and offer hope to others.
    p
      | As I work through this collection, I'm reconnecting with who he was and the values he held dear. 
      | This project is a labor of love; an effort to preserve his legacy and share his wisdom 
      | with those who knew him and those who never had the chance to meet him.
    p
      | Samuel was always willing to help others, and it feels fitting that his words might continue to 
      | offer comfort, insight, and spiritual guidance, just as they did during his lifetime.

  section.section(aria-labelledby="transcription-heading")
    h2#transcription-heading.section-heading Help With Transcriptions
    .about-cta
      p
        | If you would like to help preserve Samuel's teachings, consider transcribing one of his sermons. 
        | Many of these documents are handwritten or typed on paper that is aging, and digital transcriptions 
        | will help ensure their message lives on for future generations.
      p
        | If you feel called to contribute to this project, please email your transcriptions to the address below. 
        | Your help in preserving this spiritual legacy would be deeply appreciated.
      a.btn.btn--accent(href='mailto:transcribe@samuelsermons.com') Email Transcriptions

  section.section(aria-labelledby="whats-new-heading")
    h2#whats-new-heading.section-heading What&apos;s New
    p Here's what we've been working on to make this archive better for everyone.

    .about-updates
      .about-update
        h3 Sermon Collection &amp; Browsing
        p
          | The sermons we've scanned so far are stored in a database and displayed in a card grid 
          | with search, multi-select type filters, and collection toggles. Cards load as you scroll 
          | so the page stays fast even as the collection grows. Click any card to view the sermon, 
          | or use the share button to send it to friends via social media, email, or a copied link. 
          | There are still many more sermons to scan and add — this is an ongoing effort.

      .about-update
        h3 Bookmark &amp; Highlight Sermons
        p
          | Bookmark your favorite sermons and save highlighted passages from transcriptions, 
          | similar to highlighting verses in a Bible. Everything is saved right in your browser. 
          | Visit the 
          a(href='/bookmarks') Saved page
          |  to see your collection.

      .about-update
        h3 Light &amp; Dark Mode
        p
          | The site supports light, dark, and auto themes. Use the gear icon in the navigation 
          | to switch. If you're logged in, your preference syncs across devices.

      .about-update
        h3 Activity Feed
        p
          | Follow along as new sermons are uploaded and transcriptions are completed. 
          | Subscribe via 
          a(href='/feed') RSS
          |  to get updates in your favorite reader.

      .about-update
        h3 Transcription Workbench
        p
          | We've built a dedicated tool for transcribing sermons — a side-by-side 
          | PDF viewer and text editor with auto-save, keyboard shortcuts, and an experimental OCR assist 
          | feature that tries to read text from the scanned pages. This is helping us digitize the 
          | collection faster so the sermons become searchable and more accessible. 
          | If you'd like to help as a transcriber, reach out to 
          a(href='mailto:admin@samuelsermons.com') admin@samuelsermons.com
          |  and we'll get you set up.

      .about-update
        h3 Peer Review
        p
          | Completed transcriptions go through a peer review process to ensure accuracy. 
          | Reviewers can leave inline comments referencing specific passages, approve the work, 
          | or send it back for corrections — similar to a code review but for sermon text.

      .about-update
        h3 Points &amp; Achievements
        p
          | Contributors earn points for uploading, transcribing, and reviewing sermons. 
          | Points unlock badges from First Steps all the way up to Samuel's Scribe. 
          | There are also fun achievements like Sunday Scholar (transcribing on a Sunday), 
          | Night Owl, streak badges, and competitive leaderboard titles for top contributors. 
          | Check your progress on your 
          a(href='/profile') profile page
          | .

      .about-update
        h3 What&apos;s Coming Next
        p
          | Full-text search across all transcribed sermons, a clean reading mode for typeset text, 
          | and eventually an AI-powered tool that lets you ask questions about Samuel's teachings 
          | and get answers drawn directly from his sermons.
